                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I finished the game in about 3.7 hours and honestly, I had a great time with it. The story itself is fairly simple and doesn't try to reinvent the wheel but I don't think it needs to. It's a short, relaxing experience that knows exactly what it wants to be and sticks to it.\n\nThe visuals are beautiful but the voice acting is easily the strongest part of the game. I especially loved how consistently the Kyoto dialect is used throughout the dialogue. It gives the characters a distinct identity and adds authenticity to the setting, making the entire experience feel much more immersive.\n\nThe game also does an excellent job of capturing the atmosphere of Kyoto. From the scenery and traditional streets to the quieter everyday moments, everything comes together to create the feeling of wandering through the city yourself. It genuinely feels like a love letter to Kyoto rather than simply a game that happens to be set there.\n\nOverall, this is a short, cozy, and relaxing experience. The story probably won't leave you sitting there in silence questioning the meaning of life, but it doesn't need to. Its charm comes from its presentation, atmosphere, characters, and the little details that make the setting feel alive.\n\nIf you're looking for something laid-back that you can finish in a few hours and simply enjoy without overthinking it, I'd definitely recommend giving it a try.",
